  "id": "electromyography",
  "term": "electromyography",
  "definition": "Electromyography is a method for recording and studying the electrical activity of muscles, including at rest and during voluntary movement. In this packet, surface electromyography is described as a neuromuscular assessment tool used to examine features such as muscle fatigue, fasciculation patterns, motor unit activity, and signal complexity.",
